      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-94819",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following probabilities could be approximated using the normal approximation of the binomial distribution?\n\n1. The probability that a fair coin lands on heads $40$ times out of $100$ coin flips.\n2. The probability of getting $10$ ones on $20$ rolls of a $6$-sided die.\n3. The probability of a student getting $4$ correct answers on a true/false quiz with $5$ questions if the student answers all questions at random.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
