      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-95696",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following probabilities could be approximated using the normal approximation of the binomial distribution?\n\n1. The probability of getting $12$ defective bolts in a box containing $20$ bolts if the probability that an individual bolt is defective is $0.2$.\n2. The probability that a soccer player scores $20$ of $30$ penalties if the probability of scoring each penalty is $0.55$.\n3. The probability of getting $9$ fives on $28$ rolls of a $6$-sided die.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
